  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1225 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nSlightly cooler and drier air will filter in behind the boundary\nduring the day Thursday, as surface high pressure settles over the\nMid Mississippi Valley. Isolated to widely scattered showers and\nstorms will be possible again Thursday afternoon across southeast\nOklahoma into west central Arkansas as another mid level wave\ndrops southeastward along the eastern periphery of the ridge.\nOtherwise, dry and slightly cooler conditions will last through\nFriday over the area. Surface ridging shifts eastward for the \nweekend as the mid level ridge builds back over the Southern \nPlains. A return to southerly winds will mean temperatures warm \nback well above normal for the weekend into early next week with \nthe forecast remaining mostly dry through the rest of the period. \nThe ridge may shift far of enough east by the middle part of next \nweek, to allow another frontal boundary to come near the area, \nincreasing rain chances for at least parts of the area.\n\nBowlan",
